From 330ebfd138a003433542472927c53a167312afe2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 14sea <wanhuaning@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 21:40:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Phase 1: SD-side TPU bitstream verify (mode 't', no EPCS
 yet)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

First step of the ROT → SD-staged TPU bitstream → ALTREMOTE_UPDATE
self-reconfig flow. ROT firmware can now SHA-256-verify a TPU.rbf
loaded from a new SD slot against a golden hash baked into stage2's
bitstream-resident .rodata. Halts before any EPCS write — Phases 2-4
add the hardware (altasmi_parallel + altremote_update IP) + the EPCS
program/verify + the reconfig trigger.

Layout v3 changes:
 - host/sd_layout.py LAYOUT_VERSION 2 → 3, adds TPU_LBA=8009 +
   TPU_MAX_SEC=720 (one EP4CE6 RBF = 368,011 B). Header packs
   12 u32 (was 10), adds tpu_lba+tpu_sz at offset 48..56 and a 4th
   sha256 slot at HASH_TPU_OFF=160 (informational; firmware trusts
   only the BAKED golden).
 - host/sd_pack.py adds --tpu-rbf flag (auto-detects output/tpu.rbf)
   + 4th segment in the multi-write blob.
 - host/gen_golden.py adds 4th SECTIONS entry. When output/tpu.rbf is
   absent, emits a zero rot_golden_tpu_bitstream + warning so ROT
   stays buildable standalone before Phase 5 wires the build chain.
   Stage2's mode_t will halt on zero-vs-real-hash mismatch — safe
   failure mode (refuses an unknown TPU bitstream).
 - sw/stage2_loader/main.c: extended sd_boot_hdr for v3 fields,
   added mode_tpu_verify (reads from h->tpu_lba into 0x41000000,
   sha256_hw vs rot_golden_tpu_bitstream, halts with [OK]/[MISMATCH]
   matching existing CRTM convention), wired 't' dispatch.

Build size: 7832 → 9492 B IMEM (58% of 16 KB budget).

Plan reference: /home/test/.claude/plans/temporal-booping-raven.md
Phase 1 of 6 (~3-4 h estimate). Subsequent phases require Quartus
megawizard (Phase 2), EPCS driver (Phase 3), reconfig trigger
(Phase 4), tpu-then-rot Makefile (Phase 5), HW bench (Phase 6).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
